Replay: apply qemu-cache-maintenance.patch to pristine 11.1.1; ninja -j2
qemu-system-aarch64 in the existing configured build. Retain named executables
qemu-ic-line / qemu-ic-control / qemu-pristine-rebuilt. From repository root:
  python3 .build/floating-targeted/qemu-store-20260927/replay.py ic-line probe qemu-ic-line
  python3 .build/floating-targeted/qemu-store-20260927/replay.py ic-line static-key qemu-ic-line
  python3 .build/floating-targeted/qemu-store-20260927/replay.py ic-control probe qemu-ic-control
Full-replay.py uses the same selftest.flight and program_environment helpers,
existing matched payloads and fresh result directories:
  python3 .build/floating-targeted/qemu-store-20260927/full-replay.py NEW_LABEL qemu-ic-line
  python3 .build/floating-targeted/qemu-store-20260927/full-replay.py OTHER_NEW_LABEL qemu-pristine-rebuilt
The first candidate build lacked the arm_cpu_mmu_index spelling and did not
compile; it was corrected before testing. Final candidate/control/pristine
builds exit 0. K01/K01b/K13 remain open; installed QEMU is unchanged.
